# Claude Code's own local permission/session state -- machine-specific, not
# project config, and it drifted in here once already (an unrelated project's
# tool-permission allowlist, added inside an otherwise-unrelated content commit).
.claude/
api/node_modules/

# Local Functions settings: the storage connection string, the session secret
# and the Google OAuth client secret all live here. The README tells you to
# create it, so it has to be ignored before anyone does.
api/local.settings.json
webapp/node_modules/

# docs-index.json and search-index.json are generated by
# scripts/gen-docs-index.py and scripts/gen-search-index.py, run by both CI
# workflows before every build. Tracking them meant a 5.9MB search-index.json
# in every clone, a diff on nearly every content commit, and the two
# occasionally drifting from what the generator would actually produce
# (docs-index.json referenced lld/STATUS.md, itself gitignored, after that
# file's generation logic changed and the tracked copy wasn't regenerated to
# match). Run the generators locally after cloning — see LOCAL-SETUP.md.
/docs-index.json
/search-index.json

